<title>USA: GE/Pratt &amp; Whitney to work with Airbus - WSJ.</title>
<headline>GE/Pratt &amp; Whitney to work with Airbus - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>An alliance between General Electric Co and Pratt &amp; Whitney plans to work with Airbus Industrie to make engines for the European plane maker's proposed superjumbo jet, the Wall Street Journal reported on Thursday.</p>
<p>The newspaper quoted a spokesman for GE Aircraft Engines saying the alliance might sign a memorandum of understanding with Airbus next week in order to discuss the specifications for a new engine.</p>
<p>It said Rolls-Royce Plc of Britain was also interested in making engines for Boeing Co and Airbus.</p>
<p>Although it had already signed a similar memorandum with Boeing, Rolls-Royce had yet to sign one with Airbus, it added.</p>
<p>The venture between GE and Pratt &amp; Whitney is already developing engines for Boeing.</p>
<p>-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610</p>
